overview=dict(status='usable',rationale='Source-grounded backbone for both core relationships and their connection, with supporting membership, recovery and Ready/application paths. This is an understanding judgment, not a correctness result or exhaustive map.',
 formation=dict(explanation='A serialized RawNode caller or node.run admits Propose into raft.Step. Followers may forward; candidates or leaderless followers drop. A leader assigns term/index, appends unstable entries, queues a self acknowledgement and replicates MsgApp with predecessor identity. Followers validate the predecessor, refuse committed conflicts, truncate only uncommitted suffixes, and queue append responses. send separates these responses from immediately sendable messages. In async mode ordered durable append work releases responses; synchronous Ready/Advance splits remote and self delivery under caller persistence duties. The leader term-filters replies, requires sender progress, updates Match monotonically, computes the majority-supported index (both majorities for joint membership), and advances only if that index has the current term. Commit is propagated in appends; heartbeats cap commit at the recipient Match. Followers cap append commit at their matched request suffix. Ready exposes committed work with snapshot and application-size guards; async mode additionally requires local stabilization. Applied callbacks are distinct from Ready acceptance and client completion. Propose success promises no commitment.',behavior_ids=['B_ENTRY','B_PROPOSE','B_APPEND_FOLLOWER','B_PERSIST_DISPATCH','B_ACK_COMMIT','B_APPLY'],fact_ids=['F_ACK_QUEUED','F_MATCH','F_COMMITTED'],source_ids=['S_API','S_DOC_USAGE','S_NODE_LOOP','S_PROPOSE','S_RESET','S_SEND','S_REPLICATE','S_FOLLOWER_LOG','S_ACK','S_TRACKER','S_MAJORITY','S_JOINT','S_LOG_COMMIT','S_STORAGE_MSG','S_READY_ACK','S_LOG_APPLY']),
 context=dict(explanation='Authority belongs to a raft instance in a term and installed voter configuration. Election ticks or Campaign require promotability and no unapplied committed configuration change. PreVote can probe the next term without changing current term/vote; real campaigning increments term and queues durable self-vote support. Vote recipients check previous vote/known leader and candidate last-entry freshness. Candidates tally only the response type matching their phase, using configured voter majorities. Winning real election resets progress and appends a current-term empty entry. Higher-term messages generally install follower state, with explicit pre-vote and lease exceptions; stale messages are normally ignored. CheckQuorum may remove leadership; transfer pauses proposals and waits for transferee catch-up. Membership activates through caller application of committed configuration entries, using simple/joint transitions and retained progress. Restart reconstructs saved term/vote/commit and membership but starts follower with no leader. Snapshot acceptance checks obsolescence, follower state and recipient membership before restoring history/configuration or fast-forwarding matching commit.',behavior_ids=['B_CONTEXT','B_MEMBERSHIP','B_RECOVERY'],fact_ids=['F_MATCH','F_COMMITTED'],source_ids=['S_ROLE','S_CAMPAIGN','S_DISPATCH','S_CANDIDATE_FOLLOWER','S_LOG_COMMIT','S_TRACKER','S_JOINT','S_CHANGE','S_ACTIVATE','S_INIT','S_FOLLOWER_LOG','S_RESTORE_CONFIG']),
 connection=dict(explanation='Role reset discards vote tallies and remote Match, retains local history/commit, initializes self Match from that history and rebuilds readOnly acknowledgements. A new current-term entry plus quorum/current-term commitment reconnects retained history to new leadership. Configuration activation can reinterpret retained Match and call maybeCommit without a fresh reply. Old queued responses can survive emission, so consumers enforce term filtering; storage append completion additionally matches entry index/log term before trimming unstable memory. Snapshot completion from an older term remains processed, and application responses have term zero, reflecting committed state that outlives authority. Pending read requests awaiting first current-term commit survive reset separately from readOnly acknowledgement state: they are released only after a current-term commit and then enter the selected read confirmation mechanism. Safe reads correlate heartbeat acknowledgements by context and installed voters; returned ReadState is still subject to caller application progress. These mechanisms separate volatile support, established local decisions, durable state and externally served results.',behavior_ids=['B_CONTEXT','B_MEMBERSHIP','B_STABLE_COMPLETION','B_READ','B_APPLY'],fact_ids=['F_MATCH','F_COMMITTED'],source_ids=['S_RESET','S_ROLE','S_ACTIVATE','S_DISPATCH','S_STORAGE_MSG','S_UNSTABLE','S_READY_ACK','S_PROPOSE','S_READ_RELEASE','S_READ_QUEUE','S_ACK','S_READY_CONTRACT']),
 core_gaps=[],open_details=['Reconcile doc.go same-batch persistence/send overlap with stricter Ready interface wording before selecting synchronous driver permissions.','ReadIndex acknowledgement eligibility across configuration activation and retained pending reads needs a local discriminator.','Detailed disk failure, crash recovery and application transaction behavior are outside the captured library contract; MemoryStorage and bootstrap implementation variants remain partly unread.','Fact producer decomposition is partial: heartbeat commit and read support require separate Behaviors before a Candidate depends on them.'])
surfaces=[dict(entry_point='Synchronous Ready persistence and message ordering',disposition='deferred',reason='doc.go permits same-batch overlap whereas Ready.Messages and RawNode comments require Entries persisted before Messages. This is conflicting contract evidence, not an implementation violation.',source_ids=['S_DOC_USAGE','S_READY_CONTRACT','S_API'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='ReadIndex across switchToConfig and reset',disposition='deferred',reason='readOnly acknowledgements are context-keyed and consumed with current voters; reset replaces that state but retains the separate first-commit pending queue. Need legal membership/authority history and normative scope before a focused question.',source_ids=['S_READ_QUEUE','S_RESET','S_READ_RELEASE','S_ACTIVATE','S_ACK'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='RawNode.ApplyConfChange rejection convention',disposition='deferred',reason='RawNode comment permits no call when rejecting while doc.go describes calling with NodeID zero; selected API and application duties must be reconciled.',source_ids=['S_API','S_DOC_USAGE'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Storage implementation and external durable/apply workers',disposition='deferred',reason='Storage interface and core consumers read; concrete MemoryStorage mutations and worker implementations require expansion if selected. Actual disk durability and client response lie outside the library.',source_ids=['S_STORAGE_API','S_CONFIG'],high_consequence=True)]
mapdata=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured go.etcd.io/raft library: raft state machine, RawNode/Node adapters, quorum, configuration, log and Storage interface. Network transport, durable disk writes, application state machine and client completion are caller responsibilities.',protocol_contexts=['Per-instance raft term/role','Active simple or joint voter configuration','Log entry index and entry term','Read request context'],external_interfaces=['RawNode and Node','Storage','Ready/Advance','Async MsgStorageAppend/Apply and response messages'],ownership=['RawNode is thread-unsafe and caller-serialized; Node.run serializes its state-machine events.'],selection_injection=['Caller supplies Storage, IDs, recovered state and configuration choices; in-repository quorum and membership implementations are traced rather than treated as external.'],variants=['Sync and async storage','PreVote and CheckQuorum','Simple and joint membership','Safe and lease-based ReadIndex','StepDownOnRemoval'],source_ids=['S_API','S_CONFIG','S_NODE_LOOP','S_STORAGE_API'],unknowns=['Authentication and transport fault enforcement are outside the captured library.']),activities=activities,behaviors=beh,facts=facts,surfaces=surfaces,core_overview=overview)
Path('audit-map.json').write_text(json.dumps(mapdata,indent=2)+'\n')
submission=dict(action='research',rationale='Register the initial source-grounded formation/authority backbone and preserve precise contract and lifecycle questions before selecting a formal Candidate.',sources=sources,map_path='audit-map.json',feedback=dict(ref_ids=[s['id'] for s in sources],answered='Traced proposal admission through replication, queued support, storage release, quorum/current-term commit, propagation and application. Traced elections, term filtering, role reset, configuration activation and recovery, including the different lifetimes of entry completions, snapshots, committed application and read queues. Observations are source-based; no property execution or violation is claimed.',remaining=overview['open_details'],understanding='updated',rationale='Next compare async storage completion across term changes with safe-read support across configuration changes. The storage path has explicit term and entry-identity protections and a directly controllable ordered-worker boundary, making legal same-history checks feasible. ReadIndex/configuration has potentially wider read-safety consequences but first needs producer/consumer decomposition and an applicable request contract. Synchronous ordering reconciliation is a narrower interface discriminator that changes harness legality; retain both statements rather than silently choosing one. Prefer expanding the async completion producer/consumer map and checking a delayed old completion plus a fresh completion under a legal RawNode history.'))
Path('submission.json').write_text(json.dumps(submission,indent=2)+'\n')
